    "created_at": "2015-11-20T11:07:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-20T11:07:20Z",
    "body": "My problem with returning false if no supported tokens is present is that `add()` will always return false for things like `classList` and will return false for `<a rel>`'s `relList` on every value.\n\nWhat would happen if one day we'd want to add supported tokens to `<a rel>`? There would be no way of telling if an attribute is really _not_ supported. (whereas as defined today you can tell, even if in a cumbersome way)\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
